# Auth session stability

Read before changing auth, search, account storage, or any debounced API call from text inputs.

## Session clearing

- Only clear the signed-in user after a confirmed auth failure (`401`, `419`, `UNAUTHENTICATED`, `CSRF_MISMATCH`) from an intentional session check (`/api/me`) or explicit sign-out.
- Never clear the session on transient API errors (`429`, `5xx`, network). Surface an error and keep the current user.
- Secondary endpoints (search, conversations, messages) must never trigger sign-out. Catch errors locally and show empty or retry UI.

## Background refresh

- Session refresh runs on bootstrap and when the active account changes only. Do not tie refresh to account profile sync or other state that updates frequently.
- Profile sync to localStorage must no-op when display name, avatar, and label are unchanged. Avoid recreating the accounts array on every `/api/me` success.

## Tests required

- Add or extend tests when touching auth refresh, search, or account storage:
  - Frontend: profile sync no-op, refresh preserves user on transient errors.
  - Backend: authenticated user can hit `/api/search` repeatedly without losing `/api/me`.
- Run the full PHP and Jest suites before push.

## Smoke after auth or search changes

- Sign in on https://gocha.ai/
- Type in global search on Chats for several characters; confirm you stay signed in.
- Open a conversation, search in chat; confirm you stay signed in.
